Key Interview / OA Takeaways

Question 1

The important idea is:

Build the lexicographically smallest answer from left to right while never choosing a character that makes completing a valid selection impossible.

The feasibility check is what makes the greedy choice safe.

Question 2

The key transformation is:

lo <= max - min <= hi

becomes:

count(max - min <= hi)
-
count(max - min <= lo - 1)

Then monotonic deques allow the maximum and minimum of the current sliding window to be maintained in O(1) amortized time per element.

